@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Feature 002 - Activity and Startup Recovery
[*] --> Boot
state "Open DB / migrate / check\nrestore durable state" as Boot
state "Unavailable\nnever replace with blank DB" as Unavailable
state "No current activity" as Empty
state "Waiting\nstudents get no questions" as Waiting
state "Active\naccept complete first answers" as Active
state "Ended\nfrozen results + durable job" as Ended
Boot --> Unavailable : DB/schema/integrity failure
Boot --> Empty : no occupied slot
Boot --> Waiting : saved waiting
Boot --> Active : saved active\nautomatic, no teacher action
Boot --> Ended : saved ended\nunfinished writing becomes pending verification
Empty --> Waiting : validated preview + create commit
Waiting --> Active : owner start commit
Active --> Active : accepted submission commit\nmonotonic sequence + receipt
Active --> Ended : owner end commit\nresults + unique job + receipt
Ended --> Waiting : next create only when job terminal
Waiting --> Boot : actual service restart
Active --> Boot : actual service restart
Ended --> Boot : actual service restart
note right of Active
Stable activity URL and participant digest survive restart.
Old accepted answers / group names / sequence remain.
Student recovery does not wait for Google authorization.
Closing a page does not change phase.
No automatic end or writeback on restart.
end note
note right of Ended
Teacher must authorize original owner to view history.
Worker waits for original owner credentials if absent.
Completed jobs are not written again on history view.
end note
@enduml
